    1 \le y \le (r+4)\left(\frac{n}{r+1} - \frac{1}{r}\right) + 1 - n < \frac{3n}{r+1}  \stackrel{\Cref{eq:bound_x}}{<} 3x.
\end{equation}
Now, the inequality of \Cref{claim:up_sum_ui} can be rewritten in terms of $x$ and $y$ as
  \[
  2x \le \left(\frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{y}\right)(x+y),
  \]
  which we can rearrange to get
  \[
  0 \le y^2  - 5yx  + 3y + 3x = - (y-1)(3x-y) - 2y(x-2).
