By \eqref{eq:bounds_for_y}, we see that $y - 1 \ge 0$ and $3x - y >0$. Moreover,  by \eqref{eq:bound_x} we also have $x - 2 > 0$. Therefore we conclude that $- (y-1)(3x-y) - 2y(x-2) < 0$, which is a contradiction. 
This finishes the proof of \Cref{thm:large monochromatic matching}.

